  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Colour-House Programme",
    "overview": "The viewbook reads like the printed programme of a school sports day. The six CPE102 houses (Red, Blue, Green, Yellow, Orange, Gray) are flat, full-strength fields that own whole tiles, rows and sheets. Every week, member and project belongs to a house, and that house colour is how the reader recognises it. The team's own house is Green, so Green carries the cover and the midterm project.\n\nDensity is programme-like: a tight bento of square-cornered tiles on 10px gutters, heavy expanded numerals that read as a scoreboard, and plain reading text set calmly between them. Colour is never decoration on top of a neutral layout; the colour is the layout. Ink rules (3px under section heads, 2px between week rows) do the structural work that cards and shadows would do elsewhere.\n\nThe world rejects the dark glass developer portfolio it replaced and the white card grid: no gradients, no glass, no glow, no drop shadows.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Six flat house fields, painted through a single `--house` / `--on-house` pair.",
      "Square-ish shapes: 4px tiles, 2px tags, no pills.",
      "Archivo expanded black for numerals, headings and labels; Source Sans 3 for reading.",
      "Light and dark themes of equal standing; dark keeps the fields vivid on a deep ink ground.",
      "Structure from ink rules and gutters, never from shadows."
    ],
    "rules": [
